Future
Expectations
If sellers expect a fall in price
in the future, then the law of
supply may not hold true. In
this situation, the sellers will
be willing to sell more even at
a lower price. However, if they
expect the price to rise in the
future, they would reduce the
supply of the commodity, in
order to supply the commodity
later at a nigh pricе.
Exceptions to Law of Supply
